  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "php_hash_xxh32_unserialize",
    "file": "php-src/ext/hash/hash_xxhash.c",
    "description": "HashContext unserialization for xxh32 accepts attacker-controlled internal state with only a weak check (`ctx->s.memsize < 32`). It does not validate consistency of related fields (notably `ctx->s.total_len_32`). Later, `hash_update()` calls `PHP_XXH32Update` -> `XXH32_update`, which computes a huge copy length due to underflow from corrupted state and performs out-of-bounds read in `XXH_memcpy` (crash seen in `__asan_memcpy`).",
    "conditions": "In the `php-fuzz-unserializehash` harness, input before `|` is used as data for `hash_update`, and input after `|` is unserialized into a `HashContext` object. A crafted serialized `HashContext` for algo `xxH32` with manipulated internal xxh32 state (passing `memsize < 32` but with inconsistent length fields) is accepted by `php_hash_xxh32_unserialize`. Calling `hash_update` on this object then triggers the oversized memcpy/read and heap-buffer-overflow."
  },
